  "worked_solution": "The matrix $Q$ is singular if and only if $det(Q)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =3\\cdot x-x\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3x-6x \\\\  & =-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ is $x=0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
